values ('d9e0f1a2-3b4c-4e99-8f89-0a1b2c3d4e99', 'social-stratification', 'Social Stratification', 'This course examines how societies create, justify, measure, reproduce, and challenge unequal hierarchies of class, status, power, race, gender, wealth, education, health, place, and global opportunity. Students study major theories of stratification, empirical evidence on inequality, lived experiences of poverty and privilege, and policy responses. The course combines social theory, data literacy, institutional analysis, intersectionality, and public sociology.');

