  'Social Stratification',
  'This course examines how societies create, justify, measure, reproduce, and challenge unequal hierarchies of class, status, power, race, gender, wealth, education, health, place, and global opportunity. Students study major theories of stratification, empirical evidence on inequality, lived experiences of poverty and privilege, and policy responses. The course combines social theory, data literacy, institutional analysis, intersectionality, and public sociology.',
  $strajson${"slug": "social-stratification", "title": "Social Stratification", "description": "This course examines how societies create, justify, measure, reproduce, and challenge unequal hierarchies of class, status, power, race, gender, wealth, education, health, place, and global opportunity. Students study major theories of stratification, empirical evidence on inequality, lived experiences of poverty and privilege, and policy responses. The course combines social theory, data literacy, institutional analysis, intersectionality, and public sociology.", "topics": [{"id": "1d0fd5fd-ee00-4763-8284-902527ddb97e", "type": "topic", "title": "Foundations of Social Stratification: Inequality, Hierarchy, and Life Chances", "description": "This opening unit establishes the central vocabulary of the course. Students learn that stratification is not simply unequal outcomes; it is the patterned organization of advantage, disadvantage, honor, power, and life chances.", "children": [{"id": "37887119-0d64-4b2b-bafd-b2c05d2d96a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core Concepts", "children": [{"id": "476603f3-65e0-4657-bb46-f036158e1530", "type": "concept", "title": "Strata, hierarchy, and ranking"}, {"id": "09796d60-00f1-4b17-85cd-4c1ca10662c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Life chances and opportunity"}, {"id": "49e62503-bdf1-4c8c-b18d-35472e305b89", "type": "concept", "title": "Privilege, domination, and disadvantage"}, {"id": "0773f29a-bbfd-45c8-a11e-f78bb092b6c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Open and closed stratification systems"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between inequality as a distribution and stratification as a durable social hierarchy."}, {"id": "84fdaec6-ce48-490e-87ec-46db2f2308df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dimensions of Inequality", "children": [{"id": "9d25958a-bb2f-4da8-a77f-c6680ea602dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Income, wealth, status, and power"}, {"id": "886f33bf-1366-434e-a4d6-56880db3092d", "type": "concept", "title": "Education, health, housing, and work"}, {"id": "f3e6926e-0d24-4ce1-8dc3-09d983ed499f", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights, recognition, and citizenship"}, {"id": "99b28da6-24f0-4d6d-b44b-855560b63a12", "type": "concept", "title": "Local, national, and global inequality"}], "description": "The point is to see that inequality has economic, cultural, political, spatial, and institutional dimensions."}, {"id": "99afe45d-ef3b-4563-a217-adcca21dc528", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Why Stratification Persists", "children": [{"id": "8e21fd6a-92d7-4b96-8e21-f73fe90eee00", "type": "concept", "title": "Social reproduction"}, {"id": "85a29c46-117d-466a-b30c-77f6b0a94a14", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional inertia"}, {"id": "d5707ddb-bd56-4d1b-9ca3-b1d3f0b9aff2", "type": "concept", "title": "Ideology and legitimacy"}, {"id": "1f2e40e6-a3c6-448c-9ba4-358d2b802439", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative advantage and disadvantage"}], "description": "Students begin to ask why unequal systems reproduce themselves even when societies claim to value fairness."}]}, {"id": "05b55722-d85b-42f3-ae7f-f2876aaed4f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Theories of Stratification: Marx, Weber, Functionalism, Conflict, and Bourdieu", "description": "This unit gives students the major theoretical lenses used to explain social stratification. They learn to compare theories by what each sees, misses, and assumes about power and social order.", "children": [{"id": "77af1b25-c164-4abb-98b4-75373069ef36", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classical Theories", "children": [{"id": "53e8d38a-e69d-4fff-9719-b7912e1aea88", "type": "concept", "title": "Marx on class, exploitation, and capitalism"}, {"id": "b15694b3-ac7c-471c-96a7-cd35e5171560", "type": "concept", "title": "Weber on class, status, party, and life chances"}, {"id": "d2ecc4ed-a050-4888-ab93-dbb4f95a1665", "type": "concept", "title": "Durkheim on social order and division of labor"}, {"id": "bd03b4cf-8c90-4b92-8d8c-464846b8bce6", "type": "concept", "title": "Functionalist explanations and their critics"}], "description": "Students connect the course to foundational sociological theory."}, {"id": "72e39e32-8adf-4522-a21b-0635175156c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict and Reproduction Theories", "children": [{"id": "649c9a4b-485d-44c0-a56c-409d6cdd2981", "type": "concept", "title": "Power resources and conflict"}, {"id": "624a8416-4343-4209-a729-6083b3ef8ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Social closure and exclusion"}, {"id": "d1dea27c-03ad-4b63-b625-45ed98b18371", "type": "concept", "title": "Bourdieu: habitus, capital, and field"}, {"id": "24609938-e860-43b4-a478-e2cfe385395a", "type": "concept", "title": "Ideology, meritocracy, and legitimacy"}], "description": "The gist is understanding inequality as produced through domination, institutions, and struggle."}, {"id": "8516254d-bb46-4203-a5f6-5c11b2f20be6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contemporary Extensions", "children": [{"id": "bf31dfa1-3790-4a6f-8377-8b8b43e0d24e", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality"}, {"id": "f3bbbf57-f99a-4f70-b706-4095f7d6a7e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial capitalism"}, {"id": "de80902b-3b62-40e7-8f10-1f8382093921", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist stratification theory"}, {"id": "53accb76-3935-4ab7-83d0-3a770dd4c289", "type": "concept", "title": "Precarity, platform work, and neoliberalism"}], "description": "Students learn how theories adapt to race, gender, global capitalism, and new forms of work."}]}, {"id": "703a0ad2-1c3b-44d1-b831-3939816c6394", "type": "topic", "title": "Class Structure, Class Consciousness, Work, and Labor Markets", "description": "Class remains a central organizer of life chances. Students learn how work, occupations, ownership, class identity, and labor-market institutions structure advantage.", "children": [{"id": "52459171-458f-4055-8081-75b669ccd5b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Class Location and Class Structure", "children": [{"id": "c9a5a337-b46d-463c-925a-be1e36adec54", "type": "concept", "title": "Ownership and employment relations"}, {"id": "9efcd95f-1c4b-43d2-b4a6-ed01e72ebf9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Occupational class schemas"}, {"id": "94863e2b-a9c9-44c6-92fd-7669ce908006", "type": "concept", "title": "Service, working, professional, and elite classes"}, {"id": "1a53cf13-df57-4475-bf80-6ec432b51396", "type": "concept", "title": "Contradictory class locations"}], "description": "Students learn how sociologists classify class positions and why classifications matter."}, {"id": "1cd2d52d-4415-415f-a6c5-93ec3b425fbf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Work and Labor Markets", "children": [{"id": "c80c3818-4b39-48f0-b598-934eb566bc77", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary labor markets"}, {"id": "a58c08a0-db9a-459b-81ab-e9c958ad3baf", "type": "concept", "title": "Unions and worker power"}, {"id": "37ada9dd-e00d-4595-ad81-4e4fc75cffa1", "type": "concept", "title": "Gig work, precarity, and informal work"}, {"id": "2f9ad6a3-b799-4cca-ab9c-61023b8fb01d", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation and skill-biased change"}], "description": "The point is to connect stratification to wages, job quality, bargaining power, and institutional protection."}, {"id": "0e39c887-5643-473a-a7d3-f1037c4587b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Class Consciousness and Culture", "children": [{"id": "00dff824-960a-4625-9ea5-85541a4cdfc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Class identity and class avoidance"}, {"id": "d29d2a68-9d86-4327-b14a-56e38e7b0c16", "type": "concept", "title": "Working-class culture and dignity"}, {"id": "bb536694-e37d-4952-9dc3-90b6019d2c91", "type": "concept", "title": "Middle-class norms and respectability"}, {"id": "e39968f3-36fc-4c7f-bc23-2086c2721924", "type": "concept", "title": "Collective action and class politics"}], "description": "Students examine how class is lived, named, denied, and mobilized."}]}, {"id": "162848dc-254a-4b8c-aa02-f61e43010eff", "type": "topic", "title": "Income, Wealth, Assets, Debt, and Capital Accumulation", "description": "Income and wealth are related but not the same. Students learn how wages, assets, inheritance, debt, and policy create both short-term hardship and long-term advantage.", "children": [{"id": "204bfe50-9df1-47a6-9a7d-313387fcb106", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Income Inequality", "children": [{"id": "87ee9a11-da2c-4368-b0d7-afcbd9fc1b76", "type": "concept", "title": "Wages, salaries, transfers, and capital income"}, {"id": "144e3bc3-8c54-49fc-a216-8e65ef51840e", "type": "concept", "title": "Median, mean, percentiles, and shares"}, {"id": "88b97c32-4446-4167-b4da-c035b43f73f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Gini coefficient and top-income shares"}, {"id": "257263e0-d895-456a-9917-f60f995ccce4", "type": "concept", "title": "Household income and equivalence scales"}], "description": "Students learn to measure flows of money and interpret changing income distributions."}, {"id": "f1e370bc-2801-41bf-99b2-cb14a287afed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wealth and Assets", "children": [{"id": "b53262fd-db2c-47e4-9753-e56636238c41", "type": "concept", "title": "Assets, home equity, retirement accounts, and business ownership"}, {"id": "f371612a-0efd-451a-a52c-ea326b11efb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Inheritance and intergenerational transfers"}, {"id": "69e01a6d-201c-478a-840d-25164054ee51", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial wealth gaps"}, {"id": "bc435449-c5d2-4e99-a2d3-5349cc44499e", "type": "concept", "title": "Financialization and capital accumulation"}], "description": "The gist is understanding why wealth inequality is usually deeper and more durable than income inequality."}, {"id": "4b0ab4e3-2a6b-43e7-8783-706cf1f9e447", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Debt, Taxation, and Policy", "children": [{"id": "43ff1afa-e7af-41c4-847f-4c4ad9198320", "type": "concept", "title": "Student, medical, consumer, and housing debt"}, {"id": "16d3e762-e9f8-4754-b5ad-58082767c2d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Progressive and regressive taxation"}, {"id": "4e241c1a-d5b0-4abb-abf2-71bdde0d422d", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital gains and estate taxation"}, {"id": "51074c00-61ae-4f1e-b244-0d6bbd0a2477", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax credits, transfers, and public benefits"}], "description": "Students learn how public rules shape private resources."}]}, {"id": "f501d6d2-1b8c-4041-9521-4c1edc9dee06", "type": "topic", "title": "Poverty, Material Hardship, Precarity, and Social Exclusion", "description": "Poverty is more than low income. This unit examines poverty as material deprivation, social exclusion, policy category, moral judgment, and lived experience.", "children": [{"id": "632baf6a-398f-452c-9c99-d9a19e0067d7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measuring Poverty", "children": [{"id": "08825f57-606c-4228-ad7c-009f2e2b8d48", "type": "concept", "title": "Official poverty measure"}, {"id": "db9cf17e-91f0-4496-847c-503e1d22d662", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplemental poverty measure"}, {"id": "bc84293f-f1cf-4a9f-b0f9-a94f0c55db69", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute and relative poverty"}, {"id": "628f38c7-e01f-472f-911c-103bbb651037", "type": "concept", "title": "Material hardship and deprivation indexes"}], "description": "Students learn how poverty definitions shape what societies see and what policies they justify."}, {"id": "64122bc6-70eb-4e8e-867b-1daeb4f2ed73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lived Experience and Stigma", "children": [{"id": "366cf482-6b76-4bda-8f09-ff826bdf7a80", "type": "concept", "title": "Food, housing, utility, and medical insecurity"}, {"id": "cdabf273-c3d6-4e00-bae3-3a630f93ecdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Time poverty and bureaucratic burden"}, {"id": "298fcabf-4cf6-4435-85c1-268b63f7a550", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma and deservingness narratives"}, {"id": "681f8a91-6d54-479a-b29b-79e23054a499", "type": "concept", "title": "Survival strategies and mutual aid"}], "description": "The point is to understand how poverty affects daily life, identity, time, stress, and social belonging."}, {"id": "e16b2824-98e0-4819-8aed-678367ab4ca2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poverty Policy and Welfare States", "children": [{"id": "30bd8e5d-4550-4d8a-bf3e-a7377671865a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cash assistance and tax credits"}, {"id": "49845aad-5c35-4790-8c1f-a134bbb88fb8", "type": "concept", "title": "SNAP, Medicaid, housing, and childcare"}, {"id": "6b79121f-663e-44b6-bb63-4d3c0972dff5", "type": "concept", "title": "Work requirements and conditionality"}, {"id": "647d41d3-4883-41c3-a1ed-99864b24f280", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative welfare regimes"}], "description": "Students compare policy responses and their political assumptions."}]}, {"id": "e466d99a-ec4b-4459-a9c9-7e73ce782641", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Mobility, Opportunity, Inheritance, and the Life Course", "description": "Mobility asks whether inequality is inherited or escapable. Students learn how families, neighborhoods, schools, labor markets, and policy shape movement across generations.", "children": [{"id": "a92c30a1-5115-4f38-9909-99b0cb9a7ada", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mobility Concepts", "children": [{"id": "ff2bc9a9-f8f5-4930-9ac3-47960aa2747f", "type": "concept", "title": "Intergenerational and intragenerational mobility"}, {"id": "e5c06f02-3c31-4779-920a-f57d9e7b7d90", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute and relative mobility"}, {"id": "f70266f2-02ed-4e19-a999-6e6a93e568c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange and structural mobility"}, {"id": "7e05299d-52f1-4104-a552-9ba58874efbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobility tables and transition matrices"}], "description": "Students learn key distinctions that prevent vague claims about the American Dream or meritocracy."}, {"id": "0d703efc-bcee-47a1-862f-a7e26b7c3fdb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Opportunity and Inheritance", "children": [{"id": "c388635a-3be3-4888-aabc-aade2acebcb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Wealth transfers and inheritance"}, {"id": "70a0e467-2e34-4345-ba11-99ba1adc0f3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Social capital and networks"}, {"id": "a7cd81ba-325c-4024-8ae2-89e185dae9fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural capital and expectations"}, {"id": "f70c6d7a-2805-4ae1-85f5-0ed9b8b70dd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Elite reproduction"}], "description": "The gist is understanding how family resources transmit advantage."}, {"id": "f3cff3ac-0069-4ce7-81bc-5cef65eb9c7e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Life Course and Turning Points", "children": [{"id": "cfa56fde-654c-41ed-9431-e5888e104731", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive periods and cumulative exposure"}, {"id": "9a843f45-5e7c-41fd-bcee-f77e2c8cb1d6", "type": "concept", "title": "School transitions"}, {"id": "cd138c2b-4413-413b-893e-4d4cb67549b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Job loss, illness, and family disruption"}, {"id": "0526ca9b-15fa-4f2c-a3d3-b905a82c01fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Retirement, aging, and late-life inequality"}], "description": "Students learn how advantage accumulates across childhood, education, work, family, and aging."}]}, {"id": "1e0a8478-c4b3-47ea-97f1-c4fca13c5aca", "type": "topic", "title": "Education, Credentialing, Cultural Capital, and Inequality Reproduction", "description": "Education is often presented as the solution to inequality, but it can also reproduce it. Students learn how schools sort, certify, socialize, and stratify.", "children": [{"id": "a8fe27f6-36e3-4210-be68-e8bdcca6678f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Schooling and Opportunity", "children": [{"id": "675d4152-a7fd-4ce7-a944-55ec09b1ad43", "type": "concept", "title": "Educational attainment"}, {"id": "cf9b6b8f-c31e-4975-8577-afb0f9018dea", "type": "concept", "title": "School funding and resource inequality"}, {"id": "f44eb36f-4a85-47c4-a2ba-a3af20ea2bab", "type": "concept", "title": "Tracking and ability grouping"}, {"id": "d79cf41d-f90b-4683-8d87-55c7b092ff6a", "type": "concept", "title": "College access and completion"}], "description": "Students examine the promise and limits of education as a mobility engine."}, {"id": "e8040bec-2429-4d77-a2d6-4f723c1fc8e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Credentials and Labor Markets", "children": [{"id": "26de763d-396d-40e2-810f-0c5f0de89381", "type": "concept", "title": "Credential inflation"}, {"id": "7f5f3f1b-04a4-4231-8490-ce50f29ef90e", "type": "concept", "title": "Selective institutions and prestige"}, {"id": "507915c4-110e-423b-ab4c-d459ee0b53f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Student debt"}, {"id": "2d91e6e7-de29-48b2-a7ca-006a2d7d69fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns to education by race, gender, and class"}], "description": "The point is to understand how diplomas become signals, gates, and class boundaries."}, {"id": "d26a5273-4778-43c6-b307-7b5a3acbea2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural Capital and Hidden Curriculum", "children": [{"id": "c6c23688-d259-4674-b453-f8be5e61bcb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Concerted cultivation and natural growth"}, {"id": "81fcddda-ffe9-45d1-b2a3-2e939f7d285b", "type": "concept", "title": "Teacher expectations"}, {"id": "ae8dfba3-0724-4956-8cd4-f810417abc73", "type": "concept", "title": "Norms of professionalism and language"}, {"id": "fedc9534-9603-4471-b24e-ab55267e47ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Belonging, stereotype threat, and institutional habitus"}], "description": "Students learn how family background shapes school success beyond formal ability."}]}, {"id": "17a812ef-5852-4617-ad1f-1ecc5a334bd7", "type": "topic", "title": "Status, Prestige, Culture, Taste, and Symbolic Boundaries", "description": "Stratification is not only material. Students learn how status, prestige, taste, honor, stigma, and symbolic boundaries organize inclusion and exclusion.", "children": [{"id": "19ac89d0-6681-4a69-9d87-0323a3f1238e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Status and Prestige", "children": [{"id": "02e36b19-bf72-4890-bc5f-6bb85a998901", "type": "concept", "title": "Status groups"}, {"id": "06637088-cbec-43a4-996a-c747369744f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Occupational prestige"}, {"id": "7eacf7c1-9e5f-4443-b9df-38db71fe390c", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectability and honor"}, {"id": "763f6db0-f261-4688-a16d-165ffc4b4302", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma and spoiled identity"}], "description": "Students learn Weber's insight that honor and social standing stratify people beyond class alone."}, {"id": "3b899e11-b21a-404e-a670-8f5f95d84dda", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Culture and Taste", "children": [{"id": "1cc4e04f-781a-4ddd-9c0a-c83023d34868", "type": "concept", "title": "Bourdieu and distinction"}, {"id": "9239c0ba-fb5a-46f7-878e-a8e40880e83e", "type": "concept", "title": "Highbrow, middlebrow, and popular culture"}, {"id": "96178fda-c333-44de-b081-fe7988baa602", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural omnivorousness"}, {"id": "5052cb17-92f7-49e5-84b5-ebb261a5a413", "type": "concept", "title": "Aesthetic judgment and class reproduction"}], "description": "The gist is understanding how preferences can become social boundaries."}, {"id": "582cc336-2b56-4b8f-9686-8f89b537a737", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Symbolic Boundaries", "children": [{"id": "d58025aa-98a8-424a-8066-00a34c6bedca", "type": "concept", "title": "Deserving and undeserving categories"}, {"id": "1a70937b-1f8e-43c4-affb-507057eb7160", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral boundaries"}, {"id": "dff8c933-4344-4903-b1a9-59e0859a281c", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary work in everyday interaction"}, {"id": "ba0f668b-97b6-497e-9e8a-9dab01ece496", "type": "concept", "title": "Recognition, misrecognition, and dignity"}], "description": "Students learn how people draw moral, cultural, and social lines between groups."}]}, {"id": "062b5448-85b3-4e0a-982a-dee76fc0ed3c", "type": "topic", "title": "Power, Elites, Organizations, the State, and Institutional Advantage", "description": "This unit treats inequality as institutional power. Students learn how elites, organizations, laws, markets, and states create durable advantage.", "children": [{"id": "e529af0f-d8a4-4aa7-bd0f-2a2ae6281316", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Elites and Power", "children": [{"id": "ece4ff4f-783b-4f5e-917d-0fb5483ca37a", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic, political, professional, and cultural elites"}, {"id": "2c3ab972-c495-405a-a7da-e609cb058459", "type": "concept", "title": "Elite schools and networks"}, {"id": "4ee9bd2e-e79d-4226-8e84-4808173b054e", "type": "concept", "title": "Corporate power and boards"}, {"id": "3bbdf164-c690-45e3-a763-f1d198cf109d", "type": "concept", "title": "Power elite and ruling-class debates"}], "description": "Students learn how concentrated resources shape decision-making and social structure."}, {"id": "bb2458bc-6d0a-4130-8006-312751dc2b99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Organizations and Institutions", "children": [{"id": "beb5767c-9878-4721-bb84-b2f0b799b5ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Hiring, promotion, and evaluation systems"}, {"id": "e34eac32-6bab-4c3e-beb0-c88df85a0668", "type": "concept", "title": "Organizational inequality"}, {"id": "be007e47-56ec-4de7-a44f-dff2147fb53c", "type": "concept", "title": "Credential screens and gatekeeping"}, {"id": "bc1e46b1-6610-496c-b714-c06e83c2fd66", "type": "concept", "title": "Discrimination and institutional drift"}], "description": "The point is to understand how inequality is built into rules and routines."}, {"id": "cf93ffe7-7cb0-4f11-a683-17765c2665c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "State Policy and Inequality by Design", "children": [{"id": "4ab71db7-776c-4d85-999c-bf88f1dce176", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax policy and redistribution"}, {"id": "7e9d162c-55b2-44ef-84c0-1c9b348c1cae", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor law and social insurance"}, {"id": "bb607ba9-7af0-4b75-9584-ed12747e16c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Housing and zoning"}, {"id": "76d6b01d-888e-42ab-b774-1b3bb7cd6554", "type": "concept", "title": "Welfare, punishment, and citizenship policy"}], "description": "Students learn that distributions are shaped by law, budgets, and public choices."}]}, {"id": "f30d8a6c-cfd7-4d84-9f1a-4b6dd43ed5bc", "type": "topic", "title": "Race, Gender, Class, Intersectionality, and Structural Inequality", "description": "Intersectionality prevents one-axis explanations. Students learn how race, gender, class, sexuality, disability, immigration status, and citizenship combine through institutions.", "children": [{"id": "fa5bdc1e-63dd-429f-9039-3a66781a696b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intersectional Frameworks", "children": [{"id": "2ec33cbe-7a6f-4d3e-8444-d9ad9ab4d6d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Matrix of domination"}, {"id": "c5ae61eb-049b-4604-acd6-eda5818e8bcc", "type": "concept", "title": "Mutually constitutive systems"}, {"id": "a3af4101-75b8-4e55-b863-5e1f24e8ddab", "type": "concept", "title": "Experience and structure"}, {"id": "0bf0afff-ede1-4b62-9372-723b559f606a", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectional research design"}], "description": "Students learn intersectionality as an analytic method, not simply a list of identities."}, {"id": "74e5a60c-f88b-4e4e-9029-22fd0d1642cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Race and Structural Inequality", "children": [{"id": "6878e5d9-93ca-4fca-bb8e-4d2105cce134", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial formation"}, {"id": "8dc1ba42-e250-41da-aa49-bd68ab379d0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial capitalism"}, {"id": "1fd71612-583f-4014-aeec-a152788ea775", "type": "concept", "title": "Residential segregation and wealth"}, {"id": "cc4aeb74-4be3-4b30-8d00-3a47d9c7ac26", "type": "concept", "title": "Discrimination, policing, and law"}], "description": "The gist is understanding race as institutionally produced rather than merely attitudinal."}, {"id": "ff64d507-5972-4e04-a078-a99c9234428c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gendered and Sexual Inequality", "children": [{"id": "ec243aa7-ab40-4c53-ba18-4fa5b4bca47a", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender wage gap and occupational segregation"}, {"id": "38261dbb-5cfe-44c0-8c9f-c1a9863116c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Care work and unpaid labor"}, {"id": "81338100-a7e9-45d6-a3ea-b447fd286528", "type": "concept", "title": "LGBTQ+ inequality"}, {"id": "6359cade-adce-41a7-93a2-ba78157d1e16", "type": "concept", "title": "Gendered violence and institutional response"}], "description": "Students learn how gender and sexuality shape labor, care, violence, families, and institutions."}]}, {"id": "37fe2528-85c5-4d4e-8062-a15b182e0814", "type": "topic", "title": "Space, Housing, Neighborhoods, Segregation, and Place-Based Inequality", "description": "Where people live shapes opportunity. Students learn how neighborhoods, housing markets, segregation, schools, policing, and environmental risk organize inequality spatially.", "children": [{"id": "f5126a52-6d67-4418-bbd9-05c9ceb9feaf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Housing and Segregation", "children": [{"id": "cc6ab332-05fc-4011-a034-dd7f27974080", "type": "concept", "title": "Redlining and lending discrimination"}, {"id": "40a4aaa5-66a3-40e2-8acd-286d42bb02d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Exclusionary zoning"}, {"id": "bd1fa21a-c5fe-411c-980c-4cb15697b5fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Homeownership and wealth"}, {"id": "cead3295-ebd5-4632-9c15-e0f992031dab", "type": "concept", "title": "Eviction and housing insecurity"}], "description": "Students learn how housing policy and markets produce racial and class stratification."}, {"id": "6c961935-0988-43a4-8ad5-292ff9c63916", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neighborhood Effects", "children": [{"id": "4aa57fa0-53c5-4434-851e-630d8fb983a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Concentrated disadvantage"}, {"id": "d740173e-facf-42ae-8bde-44962522fe48", "type": "concept", "title": "Social capital and collective efficacy"}, {"id": "f7af49d9-ee1c-4f9f-a03e-6ca28f3727aa", "type": "concept", "title": "School catchments and local services"}, {"id": "aea6f0b7-1711-4609-970a-c56e99a37400", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobility and place-based opportunity"}], "description": "The point is to understand how place structures schools, networks, safety, health, and opportunity."}, {"id": "56990712-b64e-431e-be97-7bb3dae02647", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Urban Change and Displacement", "children": [{"id": "5b5d00c9-cb54-49b3-ba87-4d156ce6d685", "type": "concept", "title": "Gentrification"}, {"id": "d17e5594-c94d-43c1-ac2d-393b10a299e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Suburbanization and metropolitan inequality"}, {"id": "d78f186a-18b1-40ab-9807-070a076bed19", "type": "concept", "title": "Public transit and spatial mismatch"}, {"id": "44aa94f5-a75e-4d28-b2da-838cc047a97b", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental justice"}], "description": "Students examine how cities reproduce inequality through redevelopment and governance."}]}, {"id": "ffe80b33-63c7-4a23-b933-31e5c9f8b3d7", "type": "topic", "title": "Health, Family, Criminal Justice, and Cumulative Disadvantage", "description": "Inequality accumulates across institutions. This unit shows how health, family, punishment, disability, and age become linked systems of advantage and disadvantage.", "children": [{"id": "39a8e6ca-5d9a-4d06-91e2-c72e1ba11a89", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health Inequality", "children": [{"id": "decec721-1825-426e-ad9c-b347a1121996", "type": "concept", "title": "Social determinants of health"}, {"id": "ab036217-f1ac-4ff3-8333-d2e77d7a4c37", "type": "concept", "title": "Weathering and chronic stress"}, {"id": "f9c404bf-b55e-4ad0-af54-8049e41a49f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Access to care"}, {"id": "3561089d-4230-42fb-a780-c7b4850d19a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental exposures and disability"}], "description": "Students learn how social conditions become embodied as illness, stress, risk, and mortality."}, {"id": "cb3f80f7-47d6-4e14-b40f-a4c1c5ec60de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family and Household Inequality", "children": [{"id": "4acd2fe0-5246-415d-8e15-a740c5c587fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Marriage markets"}, {"id": "bfb41e52-92ec-45ec-a34c-af51e6386217", "type": "concept", "title": "Parenting resources"}, {"id": "58c1c525-9fa1-4a15-97b6-30f0ac7b13f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Caregiving burdens"}, {"id": "449099fb-5852-4b80-ab20-a69588e95e52", "type": "concept", "title": "Household wealth, debt, and risk pooling"}], "description": "The gist is understanding family structure as both shaped by and shaping stratification."}, {"id": "4818b2d7-2ab7-4187-8a72-db119b62ffe9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Criminal Justice and Cumulative Disadvantage", "children": [{"id": "5574d424-a47f-4d63-b437-6836f0417dd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Policing and surveillance"}, {"id": "c8068d6e-46c9-4f3f-b262-ce6d73fcbacf", "type": "concept", "title": "Incarceration and reentry"}, {"id": "d7339478-196d-451f-931b-0d3ff64fec4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Court debt and fines"}, {"id": "82d5de5d-d4c8-45a7-ba54-93ea8212dd62", "type": "concept", "title": "Citizenship, voting, and collateral consequences"}], "description": "Students learn how punishment can deepen labor-market, housing, family, and civic exclusion."}]}, {"id": "319470e5-28bb-4110-8977-4f2c8c15a45b", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Stratification, Development, Migration, and Transnational Labor", "description": "Stratification is global. Students learn how countries, regions, labor chains, migration regimes, and colonial histories structure unequal life chances across borders.", "children": [{"id": "39b2af88-3051-4192-9770-51a224d574f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Inequality and Development", "children": [{"id": "09a25d66-cbbb-43fa-95e1-7b94ebbc7045", "type": "concept", "title": "GDP, income, wealth, and human development"}, {"id": "431bf1ad-9b4f-4489-ad12-78e6c87c10d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Global poverty trends"}, {"id": "a37f5cdf-eb1b-46d6-be28-ebee437079f0", "type": "concept", "title": "World-systems and dependency theories"}, {"id": "8d2ec7ce-5c43-4218-bd80-f5417d03e4af", "type": "concept", "title": "Development, institutions, and colonial legacies"}], "description": "Students compare within-country and between-country inequality."}, {"id": "32ccef2f-4aa5-4f7f-8592-db80e56054af", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Migration and Transnational Labor", "children": [{"id": "0806745c-5932-4fcc-b7d4-11bdbb21a929", "type": "concept", "title": "Migrant labor markets"}, {"id": "a532b0a9-01f1-45cd-8b31-e30ba379883e", "type": "concept", "title": "Remittances"}, {"id": "7398d64c-626f-4143-a813-60d26f3daa96", "type": "concept", "title": "Citizenship and legal status"}, {"id": "3cd5b41e-da37-4063-b650-e5cd6ce9a833", "type": "concept", "title": "Care chains and global household labor"}], "description": "The point is to see how labor mobility and border regimes create stratified citizenship and work."}, {"id": "211d0423-040e-441f-89ba-220275e5c716", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Production and Climate Inequality", "children": [{"id": "cc919a9a-75f0-4638-88d0-2f1269a1b8d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply chains and labor standards"}, {"id": "a3cea16d-346b-4f43-891e-e69566c298cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal work"}, {"id": "c4073ac2-4a4a-4e90-a560-f31ee16b4483", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate vulnerability"}, {"id": "d7cbcf8a-31d7-4c73-9f3f-e2c171711f9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Global cities and financial centers"}], "description": "Students learn how global capitalism and ecological crisis distribute risk and reward unevenly."}]}, {"id": "d7254cc3-f12f-477e-af3a-f5e7b5956deb", "type": "topic", "title": "Measuring Inequality: Data, Methods, Visualization, and Causal Evidence", "description": "Students need evidence literacy to study inequality well. This unit teaches measurement, visualization, interpretation, and causal caution.", "children": [{"id": "94f144b4-e041-499a-8036-6ed29d7e6be1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Sources and Indicators", "children": [{"id": "06d2b09d-9b33-408f-8dbd-19b2653a54f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Census and survey data"}, {"id": "48302148-10a2-48db-b8f6-8bd865c00371", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative data"}, {"id": "365ea06b-aec1-4991-a2df-ae21490743a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Longitudinal and panel data"}, {"id": "63ac75b1-bbfb-43e7-9bf3-9643b4103165", "type": "concept", "title": "Qualitative and ethnographic evidence"}], "description": "Students learn where inequality evidence comes from and what each source can and cannot show."}, {"id": "188516a5-91d9-42cc-b3be-7002b7c00cf1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement and Visualization", "children": [{"id": "39657d48-4a09-4e99-a51c-021ea9e6293e", "type": "concept", "title": "Percentiles, ratios, and shares"}, {"id": "f2facd0c-c331-4054-a33f-cd880fb22034", "type": "concept", "title": "Gini, Palma, and top shares"}, {"id": "433e2bbf-9c97-433c-862f-6aec433368c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Maps and neighborhood indicators"}, {"id": "2adb8264-16ad-422c-946f-1e9cab8c624e", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear charts and ethical visualization"}], "description": "The gist is learning to make inequality visible without oversimplifying it."}, {"id": "20617f5e-868f-455c-a29d-53dcedb5a89d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causal Evidence and Interpretation", "children": [{"id": "9c3d3677-749a-49cc-8f96-bf8165123c73", "type": "concept", "title": "Regression and controls overview"}, {"id": "aba2dc64-7d3f-44c6-9449-4f48e03dc203", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural experiments and policy evaluation"}, {"id": "e0e24304-35ec-4681-9dea-98770d61e5b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Randomized trials and field experiments"}, {"id": "fba32bc3-0756-4b3a-b689-ca44eff06c43", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations, missing data, and bias"}], "description": "Students learn to distinguish description, association, mechanism, and causal impact."}]}, {"id": "b1481e12-3675-4552-b7a1-edeae45b8fd4", "type": "topic", "title": "Policy, Redistribution, Social Movements, and the Future of Inequality", "description": "The final unit asks what can be done. Students evaluate policy, redistribution, social movements, labor power, institutional reform, and possible futures.", "children": [{"id": "0ccac701-5e51-4ad0-8b5d-3d7e540806ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Redistribution and Social Policy", "children": [{"id": "40dba779-4060-4c0b-8b62-3bf3826f5b83", "type": "concept", "title": "Taxes and transfers"}, {"id": "6bb17f5d-2230-4721-bdbf-cdc11d693799", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimum wage, labor standards, and unions"}, {"id": "7788be59-0eff-4681-8775-d479c4da3ac6", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal versus targeted benefits"}, {"id": "83971e70-2db9-49d7-88a5-ace5a56467d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Housing, childcare, healthcare, and education policy"}], "description": "Students learn how policy can reduce, reproduce, or redirect inequality."}, {"id": "ca8caaea-d901-457a-9860-67f86eccb6a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social Movements and Institutional Change", "children": [{"id": "1202fb59-fe08-4051-897a-eb8eda7893e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor movements"}, {"id": "2b5780cb-699b-45df-9b5e-ec03095ce18e", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil rights and feminist movements"}, {"id": "b7229c58-fabf-4c37-89ff-1ceac621cffe", "type": "concept", "title": "Tenant and housing movements"}, {"id": "dfd43c6a-5550-4f96-aed4-6da229a0e850", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy feedback and coalition building"}], "description": "The point is to understand inequality reduction as political conflict and collective action."}, {"id": "6ee0aeb9-f153-41b4-aeb1-b8ec678b9db9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Future Inequality", "children": [{"id": "5044589e-037b-47a0-ab39-e5ce08ac1bf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation and AI"}, {"id": "28eb17d2-7ba0-4bd7-a82d-71ff5d032a18", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate inequality"}, {"id": "aed3f1dd-2482-46e3-a8ed-4f822f3fc065", "type": "concept", "title": "Aging and demographic change"}, {"id": "dfc4fb58-4f3f-4ab5-b981-c12aa7bd9867", "type": "concept", "title": "Democratic institutions and shared prosperity"}], "description": "Students analyze emerging risks and possibilities rather than treating inequality as fixed."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$strajson$::jsonb,
